  "@type": "Process",
  "critical": false,
  "description": "Waste management for crewed spacecraft: fecal and urine collection, waste stabilisation, trash compaction, containment of biological and chemical hazards, and venting or storage of waste for return or reprocessing. Crew output is 0.11-0.15 kg feces/day and 1.0-1.5 kg urine/day per person, plus packaging and food residues. Proper containment is essential for cabin hygiene, microbial control, and downstream resource recovery.",
